<ConverterPage
  path="/chanakya-to-kruti-dev"
  lede="Paste Chanakya 905 text on the left and get Kruti Dev 010 on the right, once the Chanakya layout has been mapped."
>
  <h2>Chanakya and Kruti Dev are different layouts</h2>
  <p>
    Both are legacy Hindi fonts that store Devanagari on ASCII codepoints, but
    they were made by different vendors and they do not agree on which key
    carries which letter. A Chanakya document opened with Kruti Dev installed
    shows the wrong Hindi, not gibberish, which is exactly why this needs a
    real map rather than an approximation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Kruti Dev half of this conversion is already finished and tested. What
    is missing is the Chanakya side. In the meantime, the
    <a href="/">Kruti Dev to Unicode converter</a> works today.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
